## 6.1.27 (2026.10.25 12:37:35)
- found diffed: com/killcoding/file/RemoteFile.java (M) vs D:/Githubrepos/JsPlus-Core/src
- fix: RemoteFile embedded-engine adaptations - writeToDisk derives a local sync root when null; copyFrom skips the logicAccess() lock when syncRoot is null; moveTo polls 15s for copyTo completion before deleting the source
- feat: new TestClock.js suite (11 cases) - Clock facade (com.killcoding.datasource.Clock) time accessors, cross-view millis consistency, remote-clock DB gap (0ms on the same machine), AppClock static accessor semantics
- feat: config/AppClock.properties generated (Enable=true) with GetAppClockSql - tracks the DB server time via SELECT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
- refactor: TestCache.js trimmed to the canonical Console.callback + CacheArray.getObject() pattern - two/three newBuilder consoles (find / callback / insert-1000 callback-delete), readable variable names
- test: TestAll.js aggregates 6 suites (TestDatasource/TestTables/TestRemoteFile/TestDiskFile/TestCache/TestClock) - 79/79 green
- feat: new TestIdentityCard.js suite (9 cases) - IdentityCard sequence generator (com.killcoding.datasource.IdentityCard): config/datasource loading, generateId() Long + fixed-length + prefix + delimiter/suffix polymorphs, cross-instance uniqueness, invalid-length guard (error 99801), DB row round-trip and cleanup; test/IdentityCard.properties + -DAPP_IDENTITY_CARD wiring in TestAll.bat/.sh; H2-compatible identity_card DDL bootstrap (GraalJS regex-less assertions)
- build: automatic version bump


## 6.1.28 (2026.10.26 08:53:16)
- found diffed: com/killcoding/cache/CacheArray.java (M)
- CacheArray: new sweepProcessed(int count) - thread-safe head sweep; the filter loop now reclaims persisted head rows right after executeBatch and keeps its local index in sync, so a global multi-thread CacheArray (e.g. ServerLog.webLogCacheArray) no longer grows without bound under sustained write load (5000-row stress: cache size 5000 -> 0).
## 6.1.29 (2026.10.26 09:06:11)
- found diffed: com/killcoding/cache/CacheArray.java (M)
- CacheArray: added processedTotal counter + getProcessedTotal() - the filter thread now counts every processed item in a long that sweepProcessed() never resets, so a monotonic global order stays available even though getIndex() is local to the current sweep cycle (per-batch).
